  .darwin_photo_control.tsv  n=12, the landing's own binaries on the study photo,
                             re-run today at load ~2

## Known gaps (the .md carries the full list)

* Linux is NOT measured. Third shipping tier, third allocator, one matrix line.
* ONE cell. No size / quality / speed sweep on any platform.
* The photograph is measured only on Darwin — the 4.9x/5.2x platform ratio is a
  `detail`-content number.
* Single-threaded. Windows' heap is worst under contention and this encode has
  none, so the multi-threaded gap is unmeasured and presumably larger.
* No instruction counts (no valgrind on Apple Silicon, none attempted on
  Windows). Wall clock and allocator-call counts are independent measurements.
* Runner CPU models unknown; hosted VMs are shared and unspecified.
